From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 20:56:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 010/159] [ae-patch] Add layout presets, two-axis dividers and
 pane swapping to the split view

The split view (patch 0005) only laid panes side by side. This adds a layout
picker to its top bar with seven presets: 2 side by side, 2 stacked, 2+1 and
its mirror, a 2x2 grid, 3 and 4 side by side. Dividers resize columns and the
panes stacked in a column, by pointer or arrow keys. A grip on each pane swaps
it with another by drag and drop or arrow keys. Adding a pane past the preset's
slots grows to the next preset that fits; closing one shrinks to the preset of
what is left.

Panes are positioned absolutely from the layout's rectangles and rendered in a
fixed key order, so a preset change or a swap never moves an iframe in the DOM
(a moved iframe reloads and drops the pane's stream and draft).

The layout persists under the same localStorage key, ae.splitView.v1, now as
version 2 ({v: 2, preset, panes, cols, rows}); a version 1 value ({panes,
sizes}) migrates to the side by side preset with its widths. The URL adds
&l=<preset> only when the preset is not side by side, so older links keep
their meaning.

Only files patch 0005 created change; no upstream file is touched.

